From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mika Kuoppala <mika.kuoppala@linux.intel.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 17:59:32 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm/xe: Remove ifdef in DRM_GPUVA_OP_DRIVER svm subop
 checking

Always emit the DRM_GPUVA_OP_DRIVER case so the previous break is
effective and we never fall through to the default warning.
This also allows adding more subops in the future without ifdef dancing.

Cc: Matthew Auld <matthew.auld@intel.com>
Signed-off-by: Mika Kuoppala <mika.kuoppala@linux.intel.com>
Reviewed-by: Matthew Auld <matthew.auld@intel.com>
Signed-off-by: Matthew Auld <matthew.auld@intel.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20260903145952.848051-9-mika.kuoppala@linux.intel.com
(cherry-picked from commit 5a3931cdaaf0f10531687cf599b2ba04dc4935b2 linux-next)
Signed-off-by: Pravalika Gurram <pravalika.gurram@intel.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_pt.c | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_pt.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_pt.c
index 426e8a29c..a41108adf 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_pt.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_pt.c
@@ -1624,7 +1624,6 @@ static int op_check_svm_userptr(struct xe_vm *vm, struct xe_vma_op *op,
 			err = vma_check_userptr(vm, gpuva_to_vma(op->base.prefetch.va), pt_update);
 		}
 		break;
-#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_DRM_XE_GPUSVM)
 	case DRM_GPUVA_OP_DRIVER:
 		if (op->subop == XE_VMA_SUBOP_MAP_RANGE) {
 			struct xe_svm_range *range = op->map_range.range;
@@ -1639,7 +1638,6 @@ static int op_check_svm_userptr(struct xe_vm *vm, struct xe_vma_op *op,
 			}
 		}
 		break;
-#endif
 	default:
 		drm_warn(&vm->xe->drm, "NOT POSSIBLE");
 	}
-- 
2.43.0

